  (text "CONTROLLER: Raspberry Pi Pico 2 sized board (Pimoroni Pico Plus 2 recommended for its 8 MB PSRAM)\nPin plan\n  GP0-GP7    sound chip data bus D0-D7 (driven by PIO, must stay in order)\n  GP8, GP9   sound chip A0, A1        GP10 /WR    GP11 /RD (also flips the data buffer)    GP12 /IC (reset)\n  GP13       knob ADC chip select\n  GP14, GP15, GP28   SPI1 SCK / MOSI / MISO: screen, knob ADC, volume chip\n  GP16-GP19  SPI0 to the microSD card (MISO, CS, SCK, MOSI)\n  GP20, GP21 I2C0 SDA / SCL to the two button expanders\n  GP22, GP26 screen CS and DC        GP27 LED data (grid + indicator LEDs, one chain)\nEvery Pico GPIO is used. Spare inputs are left on the button expanders." (at 25.4 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 188bb0fb-b119-5c27-a779-9e6e0913e41f)
  )
  (text "Boot-time pulls: until the firmware starts, these keep the YM2612 in reset\nand stop the buffers from seeing floating inputs." (at 228.6 223.52 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid b574f953-72e3-56c0-bec9-084ec3228e41)
  )
